      "message": "this looks functionally correct, but these three new states are all basically repeated code of already existing states. i think we can probably do better by keeping a flag like pd[port].trying_source.\n\nfor example, SRC_DISCONNECTED would be:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_DUAL_ROLE_TRY_SOURCE\nelse if (get_time().val \u003e pd[port].try_src_marker) {\n  pd[port].try_src_marker \u003d get_time().val + PD_T_TRY_WAIT;\n/* Swap roles if time expired */\nelse if (drp_state !\u003d PD_DRP_FORCE_SOURCE \u0026\u0026\n         get_time().val \u003e\u003d next_role_swap) {\n  next_role_swap \u003d get_time().val + PD_T_DRP_\n#endif\n  pd[port].power_role \u003d PD_ROLE_SINK;\n  set_state(port, PD_STATE_SNK_DISCONNECTED);\n  tcpm_set_cc(port, TYPEC_CC_RD);\n  ...\n\nand SNK_DISCONNECTED would be:\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_USB_PD_DUAL_ROLE_TRY_SOURCE\nif (pd[port].trying_source) {\n  /* Check if trying source has expired */\n  if (get_time().val \u003e pd[port].try_src_marker)\n    pd[port].trying_source \u003d 0;\n} else {\n#endif\nif (drp_state \u003d\u003d PD_DRP_TOGGLE_ON \u0026\u0026\n... /* continue existing dual-role toggling check */\n\nit appears we can get away with only adding a few lines to each of SRC_DISCONNECTED, SNK_DISCONNECTED, and SNK_DISCONNECTED_DEBOUNCE with this flag.",
